Description: ask an AI model a quick question from the command line
 qq sends a prompt to an AI model and prints the answer as plain text,
 steered to be short and free of markdown. It works with any
 OpenAI-compatible chat completions endpoint (such as LiteLLM, Ollama,
 vLLM or OpenAI).
 .
 Backends are named profiles in a JSON configuration file. Piped
 standard input is added to the prompt as context, and through a LiteLLM
 proxy qq can use MCP tools such as web search, running follow-up tool
 calls until the model has an answer.
